#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186293147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f8f3989e-bde0-5b3a-8d45-08f34d330c3f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Intervals of Increasing or Decreasing Displacement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd79ef94-fcdf-58f6-aa30-5aa511cb311b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd79ef94-fcdf-58f6-aa30-5aa511cb311b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293149} :answer-field/id #uuid "21660576-1240-5665-a5f3-e25ef9579462" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293148} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2110c1da-b1a4-56c2-839d-ec6245598cd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2110c1da-b1a4-56c2-839d-ec6245598cd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293151} :answer-field/id #uuid "45b0bf94-741a-59b3-b780-9aa3ef6a0c61" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293150}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c26d8c3c-e107-52ba-89a9-ccc2af1eaed1" :question/math-academy-id "q-315550" :question/problem "The displacement $s,$ in meters, relative to a fixed origin $O$ of a particle moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by $s(t)=(4t-7){e}^{t},$ where $t>0$ is the time, measured in seconds. Find the time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x.$\n\n$t\\in (${{field-1}},\n\n{{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "If the particle moves in the direction of increasing $x,$ then its velocity is positive. \n\nFirst, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((4t-7){e}^{t}) \\\\  & =4{e}^{t}+(4t-7){e}^{t} \\\\  & =(4t-3){e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate time intervals in which the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x$, we solve $v(t)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & >0 \\\\ (4t-3){e}^{t} & >0 \\\\ 4t-3 & >0 \\\\ t & >\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the time interval in which the particle is moving to the direction of increasing $x$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (\\frac{3}{4},\\infty ).\n$$"}]}
